clueweb09-en0008-45-08488.130 Madelung's Disease Replies to a question asked about Madelung's Disease. The reply provides a good discussion of the topic. http://hvmedweb.com/mw1/qanda/madelung's_disease_medweb.htm NORD: Madelung's Disease The National Organization for Rare Disorders briefly describes this rare disorder (also known as Multiple Symmetrical Lipomatosis, Benign Symmetric Lipomatosis or Lanois-Bensaude Syndrome) and lists further reference information. http://www.rarediseases.org/search/rdbdetail_abstract.html?disname=Madelung%27s%20Disease OMIM Entry 151800 Describes the form of Multiple Symmetric Lipomatosis (MSL) characterized by a collar of fat around the neck. The article suggests the cause to be a mitochondrial abnormality. http://www3.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/htbin-post/Omim/dispmim?151800 Pathology Teaching Slide - Soft Tissue Pathology The first dozen or so entries are images of Madelung's Disease, taken with various scanning techniques. http://www.cuhk.edu.hk/med/paf/slides/soft/soft.htm The Osler Medical Journal: Images of Osler Part way down the page are two photos of a man with Benign Symmetrical Lipomatosis in the neck area. http://omj.med.jhu.edu/images/vol4/june98.shtml Tumescent Liposuction Discusses the use of liposuction in the palliative treatment of Madelung's Disease. The tumescent
clueweb09-en0008-45-08488.260 the neck area. http://omj.med.jhu.edu/images/vol4/june98.shtml Tumescent Liposuction Discusses the use of liposuction in the palliative treatment of Madelung's Disease. The tumescent method is the safest method found to date. http://www.emedicine.com/derm/topic526.htm  HOME  NEW LINKS  COOL LINKS  NEWSLETTER  RANDOM LINK  SUBMIT A SITE  SEARCH  Copyright 1997-2008 HealthBoard.com
