clueweb09-en0009-57-35062.0 [Visit Your Local PBS Station] [PBS Home] [] [PBS Home] [] [Programs A-Z] [] [TV Schedules] [] [Support PBS] [] [Shop PBS] [] [Search PBS] [logo] SEARCH Archives > November 2005 TONIGHT Lionel Richie Musician-singer-songwriter CHECK LOCAL LISTINGS Home Video Podcasts/RSS [podcast] Archives Young Voices About the Show Tell Tavis Features Mobile RELATED LINKS Ron Howard Mr. Howard's bio The Da Vinci Code Article on Mr. Howard [email] E-mail a friend November 30, 2005 [LISTEN] Director Ron Howard reflects on making Cinderella Man and finding his niche in the entertainment business. [Ron Howard] Ron Howard Ron Howard [LISTEN] [READ MORE] Academy Award-winning filmmaker Ron Howard is celebrating his 50th anniversary in the business. His impressive credits include Apollo 13, A Beautiful Mind and, his latest, Frost/Nixon. He's also directed 6 different actors in Oscar-nominated performances. Born into an acting family, Howard was a vet at age 6. He starred on
clueweb09-en0009-57-35062.130 different actors in Oscar-nominated performances. Born into an acting family, Howard was a vet at age 6. He starred on TV in The Andy Griffith Show and Happy Days and in the feature American Graffiti. Moving behind the camera, Howard co-founded Imagine Entertainment and also creates online films. Read the transcript [] December 1, 2005 > < November 29, 2005 Tavis Smiley Home Page Archives Young Voices About the Show Tell Tavis Features Published November 30, 2005 Copyright © 2004-2008 The Smiley Group, Inc. All Rights Reserved Privacy Policy Terms of Use
