clueweb09-en0007-88-16915.0 [] [] [] [A Beautiful Mind starring Russell Crowe directd by Ron Howard] [Home] [Grand Theft Auto] [Night Shift] [Splash] [Cocoon] [Gung Ho] [Willow] [Parenthood] [Backdraft] [Far and Away] [The Paper] [Apollo 13] [Ransom] [Edtv] [How the Grinch Stole Christmas] [A Beautiful Mind] [The Missing] [Cinderella Man] [The Da Vinci Code] [] [] The Gods of Filmmaking The Gods of Filmmaking is not affiliated with any of the celebrities. If you would like to try to contact them try here [] [] [] A Beautiful Mind (2001) Won the Academy Award for screenplay based from previous material, director, supporting actress, and picture. Nominated for original score, makeup, editing, and actor. This wonderful little picture documents the life of Nobel Prize winner, John Nash. The film shows his struggle to live a semi-normal life while dealing with paranoid schizophrenia and problems that he encounters with the disease. His wife and her
clueweb09-en0007-88-16915.130 a semi-normal life while dealing with paranoid schizophrenia and problems that he encounters with the disease. His wife and her love for him ends up being his anchor and ultimately the reason for his success. Its amazing how well done the film is, and how it makes you believe in what you know not to be true. Russell Crowe is amazing and was completely robbed of his Oscar. (Not that Denzel Washington was bad, but we feel like we have seen him play that part once or twice before.) Also, as a side note, Howard chose to film this chronologically, which is a pretty rare and amazing feat. (Directed by Ron Howard) [] [A Beautiful Mind starring Russell Crowe directd by Ron Howard] [] [Home] [Zeus] [Olympians] [Tim Burton] [James Cameron] [Ron Howard] [Barry Levinson] [David Lynch] [Sam Raimi] [Rob Reiner] [Ridley Scott] [Oliver Stone] [Robert Zemeckis] [Titans] [Demigods] [Gazette]
