clueweb09-en0006-89-04957.390 ... Egoyan joins LFF training scheme International News: Fest launches with 'Frost Nixon' preem -- Atom Egoyan will deliver the keynote speech at the five-day Think-Shoot-Distribute training scheme taking place at the Times BFI London Film Festival, which kicks off tonight with the world ... London fest kicks off with 'Frost/Nixon' The Times BFI London Film Festival kicked off Wednesday evening with the world premiere of Ron Howard's "Frost/Nixon." Universal's 'Frost/Nixon' has hot bow VPage: Ron Howard film debuts at London Film Fest -- The Brit film industry turned out on a cold Oct. 15 night for the world premiere of Ron Howard's "Frost/Nixon," which opened the 52nd Times BFI London Film Festival to a warm reception. Leave a Comment [Comment] More from nymag.com 8 Michael Lohan Sorry About Criticizing Samantha Ronson -- New York Magazine Gawker found this 10/27/2008 on nymag.com 6 Coco Promises a Naked Halloween -- Daily
clueweb09-en0004-72-05058.0 WHO WE ARE 4-H is a community of young people across America who are learning leadership, citizenship, and life skills. Texas 4-H is open to all youth between the ages of 9 (or 8 and in the 3rd grade) to 18. If you would like to know more about 4-H and how get involved click the information button. More Info [Home] Home 4-H CONNECT Calendar 4-H Conference Center Events & Activities Find 4-H in Your Area News [Other 4-H Sites] Other 4-H Sites [Projects] Projects [Publications] Publications [Search Texas 4-H] Search Website [Site Map] Site Map Celebrate the centennial From September 1, 2007 to August 31, 2008 the Texas 4-H and Youth Development Program will celebrate 100 years of youth development in Texas. We encourage you to visit the 4-H Centennial site and learn how you can "Make it Yours" after 100 years of Texas 4-H. More Info [Click here
clueweb09-en0004-72-05058.130 Centennial site and learn how you can "Make it Yours" after 100 years of Texas 4-H. More Info [Click here for more information about youth involvement in Texas 4-H.] [Click here for more information about adults being involved in Texas 4-H.] [County Agents link to more information about Texas 4-H.] [Link to activities that Alumni can be involved in.] [Click here to learn how you can help support the Texas 4-H Program.] SHOOTING SPORTS PROJECT [pdf logo] Project Information Sheet Printed Resources: 4-H Shooting Sports Leader’s Guide* 4-H Shooting Sports Hunting Guide* NRA/NRMA Reloading Manual* NADA Archery Instructor’s Manual* Federal Cartridge Wildlife ID Guides: Upland Birds Small Game and Furbearers Big Game Waterfowl Teaching Aids 4-H Instructional DVD and much more National Rifle Association The Hunter’s Guide * available through workshops ONLY Project Experiences: Shooting Sports Contact (unless otherwise specified): Dr. Ron Howard, Extension 4-H and Youth Development Specialist ra-howard@tamu.edu
clueweb09-en0004-72-05058.260 workshops ONLY Project Experiences: Shooting Sports Contact (unless otherwise specified): Dr. Ron Howard, Extension 4-H and Youth Development Specialist ra-howard@tamu.edu 979-845-1214 Awards in most Shooting Sports events are based upon the Lewis Class System with numbers of classes and awards determined by the registrations on the entry deadline for each age and equipment class. State 4-H Shooting Sports Games Contact: Dr. Ron Howard, Extension 4-H and Youth Development Specialist ra-howard@tamu.edu 979-845-1214 The Texas 4-H Shooting Sports Games are held every July in San Antonio at the National Shooting Complex. Match include 6 archery , 3 hunting (one with 4 parts), 4 muzzle loading, 12 pistol, 14 rifle, and 6 shotgun events plus overalls for both individual and teams. This is an open match for all 4-H Shooting Sports participants. Pre-qualification (aside from membership in 4-H and either the Shooting Sports or Field and Stream projects) is NOT required. In addition
clueweb09-en0004-72-05058.390 (aside from membership in 4-H and either the Shooting Sports or Field and Stream projects) is NOT required. In addition to the youth competitions, an adult fun match is provided as a fund raiser for the Texas 4-H Shooting Sports Committee, Inc. In 2007, a total of 1016 shooters registered for and competed in this match, our annual outdoor championships. Shooting Sports Ambassadors Contact: Dr. Ron Howard, Extension 4-H and Youth Development Specialist ra-howard@tamu.edu 979-845-1214 Senior 4-H Shooting Sports members may apply from July through the end of November to become 4-H Shooting Sports Ambassadors. A selection committee will review all documents and contact applicants prior to the January meeting of the committee. Ambassadors represent and interpret the program and the state at a variety of events, promoting the program in their regions. 4-H Shooting Sports Camp Contact: Dr. Ron Howard, Extension 4-H and Youth Development Specialist ra-howard@tamu.edu 979-845-1214 Four
clueweb09-en0002-45-18075.0 Movie News Ron Howard promises new thrills PA Entertainment [Ron Howard says Angels And Demons will be set in the Vatican] Ron Howard says Angels And Demons will be set in the Vatican Ron Howard has promised Angels & Demons will be very different from The Da Vinci Code. The director insists that while his second movie adaptation of a Dan Brown novel stars the character of Robert Langdon - played by Tom Hanks - it is very exciting and new. Ron said: "I had a really fun exciting time working on that movie, it exercised a lot of different muscles for me because it is very contemporary, really a ticking bomb kind of a story and just the rhythms and the feel of it and the look of it all kind of brand new territory for me and I enjoyed it. "It's a continuation of the Robert Langdon character
clueweb09-en0002-45-18075.130 all kind of brand new territory for me and I enjoyed it. "It's a continuation of the Robert Langdon character into a whole other adventure. This one takes place in the Vatican, behind the scenes at the Vatican, and tonally the movies are not very similar but there's Langdon and there's solving a mystery, that's what we carry from one to the other." The Da Vinci Code was a huge box office success as was the novel for Dan Brown, although it also attracted a wide amount of criticism and controversy for it's allegations about Christianity and the Roman Catholic church. Tue 13 Jan More headlines Smith anticipates Obama ceremony Oprah praises Winslet's 'globes' Laurie reveals youthful death wish Piaf inspires Biggie performance WALL-E scoops Golden Tomato Prisoner Patrick McGoohan dies Olivia Newton-John's good luck note Hustle cast love 'Sir Robert' Mirren play set for UK cinemas Oscar presenters are
