clueweb09-en0000-41-25156.130 Review (RSS) Thinking Outside the Box Office (RSS) Top News (RSS) Top Story (RSS) Where Y'at ...? (RSS) Widget Watch (RSS) Favorite Links New Orleans movie times Free movie newsletter! Free movie newsletter! Archived Posts ----- December 2008 November 2008 October 2008 September 2008 August 2008 July 2008 June 2008 May 2008 April 2008 March 2008 February 2008 January 2008 December 2007 November 2007 October 2007 September 2007 August 2007 July 2007 June 2007 Ron Howard reflects on career in new documentary Posted by Mike Scott, Movie writer, The Times-Picayune December 25, 2008 11:00AM Categories: Buried Treasure Ron Howard In the never-ending quest for cinematic gems hidden in the weekly TV listings, here's what I'll be watching (or at least recording) this week: What: "Ron Howard: 50 Years in Film," a new documentary on the child-star-turned-director. When: 7 p.m. Monday (Dec. 29), with an encore airing at 10 p.m. Where:
clueweb09-en0000-41-25156.260 a new documentary on the child-star-turned-director. When: 7 p.m. Monday (Dec. 29), with an encore airing at 10 p.m. Where: TCM (Turner Classic Movies) cable channel Why: From "Cocoon" to "Splash" to "Apollo 13" to "A Beautiful Mind," Howard's well-assembled films all share one trait: a thorough enjoyability. Here, the director discusses his career with critic and documentarian Richard Schickel, right up to his latest, the critically acclaimed "Frost/Nixon." Good stuff. RELATED LINKS • From the TP: The Times-Picayune's A-to-Z movie review archive. • From the TP: More movie news and reviews from Times-Picayune movie critic Mike Scott Tags: Ron Howard Print This Page [Print] | Send To A Friend [Send To A Friend] | Permalink (Learn More) Share: Reddit | Digg | del.icio.us | Google | Yahoo | What is this? COMMENTS (1)Post a comment Posted by MysticBayou on 12/26/08 at 8:22AM Dopey is now going after Nixon??? Just
