clueweb09-en0006-40-07309.0 Quit Smoking Welcome Guest | Login or Register Home Is Self-Hypnosis Beneficial To Quit Smoking? For reasons of health and economics, and because it is becoming more and more a social taboo, you’ve made the decision. You will quit smoking. That decision is one of the hardest decisions you’ll ever be glad you made. All and all, the decision is the easy part. It is the execution of actions necessary to achieve the result that is difficult. So you have to be prepared. One way to get prepared and stay prepared is the use of self-hypnosis to quit smoking. What is Self-Hypnosis? Hypnosis brings on a trance-like state. It is not a deep sleep. You naturally go into trances all the time—sometimes while watching TV or listening to the radio, sometimes when you are driving. You know you’ve acted from a trance state when you automatically do something without being
clueweb09-en0006-40-07309.130 sometimes when you are driving. You know you’ve acted from a trance state when you automatically do something without being aware of it. Self-hypnosis lets you bring on a trance state by focusing your awareness inward. While in the trance state you are susceptible to suggestions, which is why quitting smoking through hypnosis is so successful. How it Works You can use a CD or audiotape to bring on the trance state, or you can simply bring it on by a series of deep breathing and relaxation exercises. Once you are in the trance state, focus on suggestions that enhance your goal. Self-hypnosis CDs to quit smoking, will give your strategies to anticipate smoking triggers and substitute behaviors to respond to those triggers. Using self-hypnosis to quit smoking also reduceswithdrawal symptoms often known as the “quitter’s flu.” These symptoms include headache, cough, chest congestion, runny nose, and lethargy. In addition
clueweb09-en0006-40-07309.260 symptoms often known as the “quitter’s flu.” These symptoms include headache, cough, chest congestion, runny nose, and lethargy. In addition to the physical symptoms, the psychological symptoms are equally as troublesome. Some examples of psychological symptoms are irritability, insomnia, cigarette cravings, and the inability to concentrate. A study shows that self-hypnosis to quit smoking increases your self-confidence, strengthens your motivation, and energizes you to move forward. Nothing can provide you with a 100 percent guarantee for success—a lot depends on you. But using self-hypnosis to quit smoking either by itself or in combination with nicotine replacement products, such as patches, pills, and nasal sprays increase your chances of success by nearly 60 percent. You’ve already made the decision. What actions will you take today to reach your goal? Will you consult your doctor? Will you learn more about how hypnosis helps to quit smoking? Take the first step. You’ll be
clueweb09-en0006-40-07309.390 consult your doctor? Will you learn more about how hypnosis helps to quit smoking? Take the first step. You’ll be much happier and healthier once you do. [del.icio.us:Is Self-Hypnosis Beneficial To Quit Smoking?] [digg:Is Self-Hypnosis Beneficial To Quit Smoking?] [spurl:Is Self-Hypnosis Beneficial To Quit Smoking?] [wists:Is Self-Hypnosis Beneficial To Quit Smoking?] [simpy:Is Self-Hypnosis Beneficial To Quit Smoking?] [newsvine:Is Self-Hypnosis Beneficial To Quit Smoking?] [blinklist:Is Self-Hypnosis Beneficial To Quit Smoking?] [furl:Is Self-Hypnosis Beneficial To Quit Smoking?] [reddit:Is Self-Hypnosis Beneficial To Quit Smoking?] [fark:Is Self-Hypnosis Beneficial To Quit Smoking?] [blogmarks:Is Self-Hypnosis Beneficial To Quit Smoking?] [Y!:Is Self-Hypnosis Beneficial To Quit Smoking?] [smarking:Is Self-Hypnosis Beneficial To Quit Smoking?] [magnolia:Is Self-Hypnosis Beneficial To Quit Smoking?] [segnalo:Is Self-Hypnosis Beneficial To Quit Smoking?] [gifttagging:Is Self-Hypnosis Beneficial To Quit Smoking?] Monday 22 Dec 2008 | admin | Quit Smoking Hypnosis Leave a Reply Name (required) Mail (hidden) (required) Website Quit Smoking Guides The Easy To Quit Smoking
clueweb09-en0007-18-22204.0 [Fast Quit Smoking Header] Drug Detox Alcoholism Treatment drug rehab [My plan to quit smoking]My Last Smoke [My plan to quit smoking] Fast Quit Smoking Please let me explain a little about myself. I am now a non-smoker. I have smoked since I met my wife 32 years ago. ( I will ponder that one for a while). Anyway smoking has never really bothered me till 2004, that was the year my heart decided to throw up it's hands in disgust with me. Well since then I have tried every which way to stop, but to no avail, until now so happily I am NO LONGER SMOKING. Thanks to this program. So why should you listen to me about giving up or quitting smoking? Well I have gone through everything you are likely to ever go through while trying to stop smoking. From anger, depression, being snappy at everyone, over
clueweb09-en0007-18-22204.130 you are likely to ever go through while trying to stop smoking. From anger, depression, being snappy at everyone, over eating, cheating and lack of willpower to name but a few. Because of all this, and still being unable to completely give up smoking, I decided to really look good and hard into this somehow mystical problem I, and many others, have. I am an average guy with average intelligence and do understand all the critics and their points of view for having a smoke free world. I said I understand them but not necessarily agree with them all as there are some people out there, I am sure you have met them, that no matter what we do will say we should not be doing it. An example of them; some time ago while in the USA there was a study on handling money, specifically paper notes. The study
clueweb09-en0007-18-22204.260 them; some time ago while in the USA there was a study on handling money, specifically paper notes. The study went on to inform us that we were all at a potential risk of getting cancer from this. True or not no one stopped handling money and no more was heard from this doom and gloom crowd. The point is do things you feel are right for you not because someone else thinks it is right for you. But I digress. The reason I am still smoking now is, funny enough because I did discover the Fast Quit Smoking System myself. I applied it and after two weeks with, get this, no drugs, patches, injections or tablets (pills), I completely gave up smoking. So why am I smoking again? The same reason many are unable to give up themselves, I have a partner and son that smoke. All us smokers
clueweb09-en0007-18-22204.390 same reason many are unable to give up themselves, I have a partner and son that smoke. All us smokers know how extremely difficult if not impossible it is to stop smoking if there is someone in the household who smokes and does not wish to give up.Why was this a reason to start again you may ask, I must be stupid after giving up especially after being able to with family members smoking around me. Well actually no, I am not stupid, I have a method in my madness. Let me explain, you see my wife and son tried to stop while I was giving up but could not go through with it as they were not on my Fast Quit Smoking System. No I did not tell them what I had discovered as I was not sure it was the answer. So finally, with me smoking again, my
